!!! Routing: which handler answers a path.
!!!
!!! A route names its handler with text, and the application dispatches on
!!! that name. This is not the shape the Ny original had — there a route held
!!! an IPage object and the router called it — and the reason it changed is
!!! the language: Matrix has no capturing closures, and an array of class
!!! handles compiles but does not execute. There is no way to put a callable
!!! in a route table. A name is the thing that can be stored, compared and
!!! switched on, so a name is what a route holds.
!!!
!!! What this costs is one `switch` in the application that lists its
!!! handlers. What it buys is a route table that is plain data: it can be
!!! read, printed, tested and reordered without running anything, and a
!!! mistyped handler name is a 500 with a message rather than a crash.

book nilweb.routing.router

read nil.std.text
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.method
read everything from nilweb.http.uri


public route begin record
    field verb as request-method
    !!! A pattern is literal segments, `:name` captures and a trailing `*name`.
    field pattern as text
    !!! The name the application switches on to run this route.
    field handler as text
end record


!!! --- The outcome of matching one request against the whole table.
!!!
!!! `path-matched` is separate from `matched` so the caller can tell 404 from
!!! 405. A path no route claims is Not Found; a path a route claims by another
!!! method is Method Not Allowed, and RFC 9110 requires that answer to carry
!!! an Allow field — which is why `allowed` is here and not reconstructed by
!!! the caller.

public route-result begin record
    field matched as boolean
    field handler as text
    field captures as array of query-parameter
    field path-matched as boolean
    field allowed as text
end record


public no-routes returns array of route begin paragraph
    variable empty as array of route is []
    give empty
end paragraph


public add-route receives routes as array of route, verb as request-method, pattern as text, handler as text
    returns array of route begin paragraph
    variable out as array of route is []
    repeat for each existing in routes
        append existing to out
    end repeat
    append build route with verb being verb, pattern being pattern, handler being handler to out
    give out
end paragraph


public get-route receives routes as array of route, pattern as text, handler as text returns array of route begin paragraph
    give add-route with routes being routes, verb being request-method.Get, pattern being pattern, handler being handler
end paragraph


public post-route receives routes as array of route, pattern as text, handler as text returns array of route begin paragraph
    give add-route with routes being routes, verb being request-method.Post, pattern being pattern, handler being handler
end paragraph


public put-route receives routes as array of route, pattern as text, handler as text returns array of route begin paragraph
    give add-route with routes being routes, verb being request-method.Put, pattern being pattern, handler being handler
end paragraph


public delete-route receives routes as array of route, pattern as text, handler as text returns array of route begin paragraph
    give add-route with routes being routes, verb being request-method.Delete, pattern being pattern, handler being handler
end paragraph


!!! --- Match a request against the table, first route wins.
!!!
!!! In declaration order rather than by specificity. Specificity ordering is
!!! clever and surprising — it decides that `/users/new` loses to `/users/:id`
!!! on a rule the person writing the table cannot see — and declaration order
!!! is the one a reader can check by reading downwards.
!!!
!!! A HEAD request matches a GET route, because a HEAD is a GET whose body is
!!! discarded, and a table that had to repeat every route for HEAD would be a
!!! table with half its entries wrong.

public match-route receives routes as array of route, verb as request-method, path as text
    returns route-result begin paragraph
    variable allowed as text is ""
    variable path-matched as boolean is false

    repeat for each candidate in routes
        value attempt-made is match-pattern with pattern being candidate.pattern, path being path
        when attempt-made.matched then
            set path-matched to true
            when methods-agree with wanted being verb, offered being candidate.verb then
                give build route-result with
                    matched being true,
                    handler being candidate.handler,
                    captures being attempt-made.captures,
                    path-matched being true,
                    allowed being ""
            end when
            set allowed to add-to-allowed with allowed being allowed, verb being candidate.verb
        end when
    end repeat

    give build route-result with
        matched being false,
        handler being "",
        captures being (no-captures with nothing),
        path-matched being path-matched,
        allowed being allowed
end paragraph


methods-agree receives wanted as request-method, offered as request-method returns boolean begin paragraph
    when (method-name with verb being wanted) equals (method-name with verb being offered) then
        give true
    end when
    !!! A HEAD is served by the GET route; render-response drops the body.
    give (method-name with verb being wanted) equals "HEAD"
        and (method-name with verb being offered) equals "GET"
end paragraph


!!! --- Build the Allow field, adding HEAD alongside GET because the route
!!! that serves one serves the other.

add-to-allowed receives allowed as text, verb as request-method returns text begin paragraph
    value name is method-name with verb being verb
    value full is when name equals "GET" give "GET, HEAD" otherwise give name end when
    when allowed equals "" then
        give full
    end when
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being allowed, needle being full then
        give allowed
    end when
    give allowed plus ", " plus full
end paragraph


no-captures returns array of query-parameter begin paragraph
    variable empty as array of query-parameter is []
    give empty
end paragraph


!!! --- The outcome of matching one pattern.

public pattern-result begin record
    field matched as boolean
    field captures as array of query-parameter
end record


!!! --- Match one pattern against one path.
!!!
!!! Segment by segment. `:name` takes exactly one segment; `*name` takes the
!!! rest of the path including its separators and must come last. An empty
!!! capture is a failure, so `/users/:id` does not match `/users/` and hand a
!!! handler an empty id to fall over on later.

public match-pattern receives pattern as text, path as text returns pattern-result begin paragraph
    value pattern-parts is split-on with input being (trimmed-path with path being pattern), separator being "/"
    value path-parts is split-on with input being (trimmed-path with path being path), separator being "/"
    variable captures is no-captures with nothing

    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of pattern-parts
        value piece is pattern-parts at index
        value kind is piece-kind with piece being piece

        when kind equals "rest" then
            value taken is join-from with parts being path-parts, start being index
            when taken equals "" then
                give build pattern-result with matched being false, captures being (no-captures with nothing)
            end when
            append build query-parameter with
                name being (nil.std.text::substring with s being piece, start being 1,
                    length being (nil.std.text::length with s being piece) minus 1),
                content being taken
                to captures
            give build pattern-result with matched being true, captures being captures
        end when

        when index is at least the length of path-parts then
            give build pattern-result with matched being false, captures being (no-captures with nothing)
        end when
        value against is path-parts at index

        !!! Flat rather than nested: a `when` whose branches each hold their
        !!! own `when` needs an explicit arm block to stay unambiguous, and
        !!! three plain conditions read better than one with two tails.
        value capture-failed is kind equals "capture" and against equals ""
        value literal-failed is kind equals "literal" and not (piece equals against)
        when capture-failed or literal-failed then
            give build pattern-result with matched being false, captures being (no-captures with nothing)
        end when
        when kind equals "capture" then
            append build query-parameter with
                name being (nil.std.text::substring with s being piece, start being 1,
                    length being (nil.std.text::length with s being piece) minus 1),
                content being against
                to captures
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat

    when the length of path-parts is greater than the length of pattern-parts then
        give build pattern-result with matched being false, captures being (no-captures with nothing)
    end when
    give build pattern-result with matched being true, captures being captures
end paragraph


piece-kind receives piece as text returns text begin paragraph
    when (nil.std.text::length with s being piece) is less than 2 then
        give "literal"
    end when
    value first is nil.std.text::substring with s being piece, start being 0, length being 1
    when first equals ":" then give "capture" end when
    when first equals "*" then give "rest" end when
    give "literal"
end paragraph


!!! --- A path without its leading separator, so "/a/b" and "a/b" split alike
!!! and a trailing separator does not add an empty segment.

trimmed-path receives path as text returns text begin paragraph
    variable out as text is path
    when nil.std.text::starts_with with s being out, prefix being "/" then
        set out to nil.std.text::substring with s being out, start being 1,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being out) minus 1
    end when
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being out
    when width is greater than 0 and (nil.std.text::ends_with with s being out, suffix being "/") then
        set out to nil.std.text::substring with s being out, start being 0, length being width minus 1
    end when
    give out
end paragraph


join-from receives parts as array of text, start as number returns text begin paragraph
    variable out as text is ""
    variable index as number is start
    repeat while index is less than the length of parts
        when not (out equals "") then
            set out to out plus "/"
        end when
        set out to out plus (parts at index)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- A capture by name, which is how a handler reads `:id`.

public capture-of receives result as route-result, name as text returns text begin paragraph
    give parameter-value with parameters being result.captures, name being name
end paragraph
